[TEXT] **Root cause found.** Router6 has a live nftables FORWARD chain that **drops all traffic entering on eth2** (the `r6_r3` link — the only uplink connecting router6 to the rest of the network):

```
iifname "eth2" ip saddr 172.16.10.0/24 ip daddr 172.18.51.1 tcp dport 80 → ACCEPT (tiny exception)
iifname "eth2" tcp  → DROP  (0 pkts so far)
iifname "eth2" udp  → DROP  (18 pkts — our traceroute probes)
iifname "eth2"      → DROP  (78 pkts — ICMP replies, etc.)
```

This makes the fault perfectly asymmetric:
- **pc15→pc5 forward path**: packets leave pc15 on eth1→eth2 (no eth2 *inbound* rule applies) → reach pc5 ✓  
- **pc5→pc15 return path**: reply arrives on router6's **eth2**, hits the DROP rule → never forwarded to eth1 → pc15 sees 100% loss ✗

